# Context handoff (Auto)

Chat memory ≠ SoT. When the window is thin, mid-step, or a new chat continues work — **files win**. Do not invent NEXT from residual chat.

## SoT (read first every continue / Scout)

1. `active_context.md` — Goal · Done · Not verified · Open decisions · Next · paste block
2. `progress.md` — last QA/DevOps JSON · Next line
3. User’s latest message (overrides stale file Status only when explicit)

If (1)+(2) contradict the latest user ask → **stop** · report drift · ask which wins. Do not Builder.

## When to hard-stop (no Builder / no “finish the wave”)

Trigger any of:

- User: `context thin` · `handoff only` · `no code` · chat အသစ် / continue-from-files
- Self-check: long thread + large tool dumps + cannot restate DONE/NEXT from **files** without guessing
- Mid Scout/Architect/Builder/QA/DevOps and the next action needs facts not in files or this turn’s tool results
- **`preCompact` hook warn** (`.cursor/hooks/precompact-handoff-warn.py`) — compaction စရင် treat as thin · handoff only (hook cannot block compact)

On hard-stop:

1. Update `active_context.md`: **DONE** · **PARTIAL** (if mid-Builder) · **NEXT** · **Out of scope** · paste-ready first message
2. Update `progress.md` Next line if QA/status changed
3. Reply: short status + paste block only — **no new code** · no workflow step jump
4. End. Do not append “meanwhile I’ll also…”

## Mid-step partial (Builder/QA ကျိုးချိန်)

| State | Write to `active_context` |
|-------|---------------------------|
| Scout/Architect done | Status = plan ready · NEXT = Builder |
| Builder half-done | **PARTIAL** = files touched + what’s left · NEXT = finish Builder then QA · list exact block folders / PHP paths |
| Build run but not verified | PARTIAL = `npm run build` result only · NEXT = editor smoke test |
| QA incomplete | PARTIAL = checks run / not run · NEXT = QA |
| DevOps notes only | NEXT = user zip/install/smoke · no fake PASS |

Never mark Visual / QA **PASS** without evidence in this turn or `progress.md`.
A green `npm run build` alone is **not** a QA PASS — editor render + block validation are separate.

## Release-state drift (project-specific)

Version lives in three places — `twork-builder.php` header + `TWORK_BUILDER_VERSION`, `readme.txt` stable tag, `package.json`.
On any handoff mid-release, record all three actual values in `active_context.md`. Never assume they match.

## New chat / continue paste (agent must emit or refresh)

Keep a fenced paste under `active_context.md` “Context ကုန်လို့ နောက် chat” (or equivalent):

```
Continue twork-builder from active_context.md + progress.md.
DONE: …
NEXT: …
SoT / rejects / wave limits…
If context thin: update active_context handoff only — no code.
Workflow Scout→… one step per y.
```

New chat turn 1 = **Scout from files** (or handoff-only if the user said so). Do not skip to Builder because “we were about to”.

## Workflow lock (unchanged)

- One numerical step per user `y`
- Do not run Builder+QA in the same turn as Scout/Architect
- `y` alone after a handoff ≠ permission to guess a missing NEXT — re-read files first

## Reject

- Continuing implementation from chat recall when `active_context` Status/NEXT is missing or stale
- Inventing block names, attribute names, versions, PASS, or “probably done”
- Expanding scope to “finish while we’re here” under thin context
- Replacing this rule with a Skill (session hygiene stays always-on `.mdc`)
